      "description": "The (Vowel + Consonant)உயிர்மெய் எழுத்துக்கள் are compound letters in Tamil formed by combining a consonant (மெய்) with a vowel (உயிர்). For example, the consonant ண்(N) combines with vowels to form ண, ணா, ணி, ணீ, ணு, ணூ, ணெ, ணே, ணை, ணொ, ணோ, and ணௌ."
